[Event "02. Side by side: the king cannot stop both (1/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/k1PP4/8/8/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. Side by side: the king cannot stop both (1/8)"]
[LineDescription "Side by side: push the pawn the king cannot reach; it cannot stop both."]

{[%csl Gc8,Gd8,Ba7,Bb6,Bb5,Ba5] Two pawns side by side guard the squares in
front of each other. When the black king comes up beside them, push the pawn it
cannot reach: it cannot stop both, and your own king does not even need to help.
The black king is next to your pawns. Which pawn goes forward? Green: the
queening squares. Blue: the squares the black king can step to.} 1. d7 {The
d-pawn goes: the black king is too far from d8 to stop it.} 1... Kb5 {[%csl
Gd8,Gc8,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bc5,Bc4,Bb4,Ba4,Ba5]} 2. d8=Q {Queen! The black king is too
far away to take the new queen. With a queen, the win is easy from here.} *

