[Event "03. If the king takes one, the other runs (1/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/K7/8/8/k1P5/3P4/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "03. If the king takes one, the other runs (1/8)"]
[LineDescription "If the king takes one pawn, the other runs: push the pawn that is out of its reach."]

{[%csl Gd3,Gd4,Gd5,Gd6,Gd7,Gd8,Rc3] The black king can win one of your pawns.
Let it! While it is busy taking one, the other pawn runs to the queening square,
and the king is too far behind to catch it. Push the right pawn and count the
moves. The black king is close to your pawns. Push the pawn that runs away from
it. Green: the runner's way to the queening square. Red: the pawn the king is
going to take.} 1. d4 {Push the runner! The king may take the c-pawn, but then
the d-pawn is too far ahead for it.} 1... Kb2 {[%csl Gd5,Gd6,Gd7,Gd8,Rc3] The
king attacks the pawn on c3!} 2. d5 {Forward again: the king is busy with the
other pawn.} 2... Kxc3 {[%csl Gd6,Gd7,Gd8] The king takes the pawn on c3, but
now the d-pawn runs, and the king is too far behind to catch it.} 3. d6 {The
d-pawn goes: the black king is too far from d8 to stop it.} 3... Kb4 {[%csl
Gd7,Gd8]} 4. d7 {The d-pawn keeps running.} 4... Kc5 {[%csl Gd8]} 5. d8=Q
{Queen! The black king is too far away to take the new queen. With a queen, the
win is easy from here.} *

