[LineName "03. If the king takes one, the other runs (8/8)"]
[LineDescription "If the king takes one pawn, the other runs: push the pawn that is out of its reach."]

{[%csl Gc5,Gc6,Gc7,Gc8,Rb3] The king will take one pawn. Make sure it is the
slow one.} 1. c5 {Push the runner! The king may take the b-pawn, but then the
c-pawn is too far ahead for it.} 1... Kb2 {[%csl Gc6,Gc7,Gc8,Rb3] The king
attacks the pawn on b3!} 2. c6 {Forward again: the king is busy with the other
pawn.} 2... Kxb3 {[%csl Gc7,Gc8] The king takes the pawn on b3, but now the
c-pawn runs, and the king is too far behind to catch it.} 3. c7 {The c-pawn
goes: the black king is too far from c8 to stop it.} 3... Kc4 {[%csl Gc8]} 4.
c8=Q+ {Queen! The black king is too far away to take the new queen. With a
queen, the win is easy from here.} *

[Event "04. The chain protects itself: bring your king (1/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/4k3/4P3/5P2/K7/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. The chain protects itself: bring your king (1/8)"]
[LineDescription "The chain holds on its own: the pawns wait while the king walks over to help."]

{[%csl Gd7,Be7,Bf7,Bf5,Bd5] With the black king in front of them, two pawns
cannot promote on their own. But they do not need help to survive: the back pawn
protects the front one, and when the king goes for the back pawn, the front one
runs. So the pawns wait, and your king walks over to help. The black king blocks
your pawns. They can wait: bring your king. Blue: the squares the black king can
step to. Green: where your king is heading.} 1. Kb4 {The pawns hold on their
own: the king cannot take the e-pawn, the f-pawn protects it. So your king walks
over to help: it is heading for d7, 3 steps away.} 1... Kd5 {[%csl
Gd7,Bc6,Be6,Be4,Bd4]} 2. Kb5 {The king keeps walking: 2 steps from d7.} 2... Ke6
{[%csl Gd7,Be7,Bf7,Bf5,Bd5]} 3. Kc6 {The king keeps walking: 1 step from d7.}
3... Ke7 {[%csl Gd7,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bf7,Be6]} 4. Kc7 {Your king goes round: the
black king guards d7.} 4... Ke6 {[%csl Gd7,Be7,Bf7,Bf5,Bd5]} 5. Kd8 {Your king
goes round: the black king guards d7.} 5... Kd5 {[%csl
Gd7,Bc6,Be6,Be4,Bd4,Bc4,Bc5]} 6. Kd7 {The king has arrived on d7: now the pawns
can move up.} 6... Kd4 {[%csl Bc5,Bd5,Be4,Be3,Bd3,Bc3,Bc4]} 7. e6 {The e-pawn
moves up, protected by your king.} 7... Kd5 {[%csl Be4,Bd4,Bc4,Bc5]} 8. e7 {The
e-pawn reaches the 7th rank, protected by your king: one more step.} 8... Kc5
{[%csl Bb6,Bd5,Bd4,Bc4,Bb4,Bb5]} 9. e8=Q {Queen! Your king protects the new
queen. With a queen, the win is easy from here.} *

