[LineName "05. Escort them with your king (10/10)"]
[LineDescription "The king takes squares from the black king; the pawns move up when it is safe."]

{[%csl Ge8,Be7,Bd7,Bc7,Bc8] Your king is next to the pawns. Bring them home.} 1.
Ke6 {The king goes ahead of the pawns: it clears the way and takes squares from
the black king.} 1... Kc7 {[%csl Ge8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Bc6,Bb6,Bb7]} 2. e5 {The e-pawn
moves up, protected by your king.} 2... Kc6 {[%csl Ge8,Bb7,Bc7,Bc5,Bb5,Bb6]} 3.
Kf7 {The king leads the way again.} 3... Kd5 {[%csl Ge8,Bc6,Be5,Bd4,Bc5] The
king attacks the pawn on e5!} 4. e6 {Up again, protected by your king.} 4... Ke5
{[%csl Ge8,Bd6,Bf5,Bf4,Bd4,Bd5]} 5. e7 {The e-pawn reaches the 7th rank,
protected by your king: one more step.} 5... Kd6 {[%csl
Ge8,Bc7,Bd7,Be5,Bd5,Bc5,Bc6]} 6. e8=Q {Queen! Your king protects the new queen.
With a queen, the win is easy from here.} *

[Event "06. Don't stalemate! (1/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "k7/2K5/8/1P6/2P5/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Don't stalemate! (1/6)"]
[LineDescription "Before a quiet move near the corner, check that the black king still has a move."]

{[%csl Ba7] [%cal Rb5b6] Near the edge, the lone king is often short of squares.
Before every move ask: does the black king still have a move? If it has none and
is not in check, it is stalemate, and the game is only a draw. The black king is
in the corner with hardly a square. One careless move and it is stalemate. Blue:
the squares the black king can step to. Red arrow: a natural move that would be
stalemate.} 1. c5 {Not b6: that leaves the black king without a move, and it is
stalemate! The c-pawn moves up.} 1... Ka7 {[%csl Ba8]} 2. b6+ {Check! The pawn
drives the black king back.} 2... Ka6 {[%csl Bb5,Ba5]} 3. b7 {The b-pawn reaches
the 7th rank, protected by your king: one more step.} 3... Ka7 {[%csl Ba6]} 4.
b8=Q+ {Queen! Your king protects the new queen. With a queen, the win is easy
from here.} *

[Event "06. Don't stalemate! (2/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "5k2/5P2/6P1/6K1/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Don't stalemate! (2/6)"]
[LineDescription "Before a quiet move near the corner, check that the black king still has a move."]

{[%csl Bg7,Be7] [%cal Rg5f6] Short of squares again: leave the king a move.} 1.
Kh6 {Not Kf6: that leaves the black king without a move, and it is stalemate! A
king move: the pawns stay protected, and now Black has to move.} 1... Ke7 {[%csl
Bd8,Bf8,Bf6,Be6,Bd6,Bd7]} 2. Kg7 {Your king guards f8: now the pawn can promote
safely.} 2... Ke6 {[%csl Bd7,Be7,Bf5,Be5,Bd5,Bd6]} 3. f8=Q {Queen! Your king
protects the new queen. With a queen, the win is easy from here.} *

[Event "06. Don't stalemate! (3/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3k4/3P4/2P5/2K5/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Don't stalemate! (3/6)"]
[LineDescription "Before a quiet move near the corner, check that the black king still has a move."]

{[%csl Be7,Bc7] [%cal Rc5d6] Count the black king's squares before you move.} 1.
Kb6 {Not Kd6: that leaves the black king without a move, and it is stalemate! A
king move: the pawns stay protected, and now Black has to move.} 1... Ke7 {[%csl
Bd8,Bf8,Bf7,Bf6,Be6,Bd6]} 2. Kc7 {Your king guards d8: now the pawn can promote
safely.} 2... Ke6 {[%csl Be7,Bf7,Bf6,Bf5,Be5,Bd5]} 3. d8=Q {Queen! Your king
protects the new queen. With a queen, the win is easy from here.} *

[Event "06. Don't stalemate! (4/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "7k/8/4PP1K/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Don't stalemate! (4/6)"]
[LineDescription "Before a quiet move near the corner, check that the black king still has a move."]

{[%csl Bg8] [%cal Rf6f7] Short of squares again: leave the king a move.} 1. e7
{Not f7: that leaves the black king without a move, and it is stalemate! The
e-pawn reaches the 7th rank, protected by the f-pawn: one more step.} 1... Kg8
{[%csl Bh8,Bf7]} 2. e8=Q# {Queen! The black king is too far away to take the new
queen, and it is even checkmate!} *

[Event "06. Don't stalemate! (5/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "k1K5/8/1P6/P7/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Don't stalemate! (5/6)"]
[LineDescription "Before a quiet move near the corner, check that the black king still has a move."]

{[%cal Rc8c7,Ra5a6] Count the black king's squares before you move.} 1. b7+ {Not
Kc7 or a6: each of them leaves the black king without a move, and it is
stalemate! Check! The pawn drives the black king back.} 1... Ka7 {[%csl Ba6]} 2.
b8=Q+ {Queen! Your king protects the new queen. With a queen, the win is easy
from here.} *

[Event "06. Don't stalemate! (6/6)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/1P6/2P5/8/8/8/8/5K1k w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "06. Don't stalemate! (6/6)"]
[LineDescription "If a new queen would be stalemate, take a rook: it wins just as surely."]

{[%csl Bh2] Promote right now, but count the black king's squares first.} 1.
b8=R {Rook! A new queen would have taken the black king's last square:
stalemate. The rook leaves it a square, and the rook wins just as surely.} *

